    given-names: "Sizhe"

type: software

abstract: >-
  The Structural Intelligence Compass is an open research framework for
  examining intelligence, computation, reasoning, organization, and their
  boundaries from twelve structural directions. Version 0.2.0 preserves
  the original 12-Point Compass as the research baseline while adding a
  Post-Release Structural Delta through the Additional Thoughts series.
  The new material develops Structural Differential Computation,
  Calling-Path Folding as a recurring computational pattern, Enumerative
  Structure as a computational possibility space, Local Learned
  Intelligence and Grounded Structural IR, Technology Convergence and
  Policy Surfaces, and a candidate synthesis direction toward
  Policy-Driven Structural Hybrid Intelligence. The release further
  distinguishes Problem Space from Intelligence Space, expands Per-Node
  Intelligence beyond single-model architectures, and develops the
  progression from Structural Discovery through Structural Synthesis
  toward Structural Evolution. Point 12 remains intentionally open and
  is not treated as having reached a final definition.

